{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And you shall bring there, inside the veil, the ark of the testimony.</b> He is not now commanding us to act in this sequence — that he place the veil under the clasps and afterward bring there, inside the veil, the ark — for the command here is not concerning the erection of the Tabernacle but concerning its making. And likewise (Exodus 26:34) <b>and you shall place the cover upon the ark of the testimony in the Holy of Holies</b> — its meaning is not that he should place the cover upon the ark of the testimony while the ark is already there in the Holy of Holies. Rather, the matter is that Scripture commands him to place the veil under the clasps so that the ark should be there inside the veil, and the veil shall separate between the Holy and the Holy of Holies. And likewise it says <b>and you shall place the cover upon the ark of the testimony in the Holy of Holies</b> to inform that the cover with its cherubim upon the ark shall all be there in the Holy of Holies, which was mentioned — that is, inside the veil. But when it arrives at the command for its erection, it says <b>and you shall place there the ark of the testimony</b> (Exodus 40:3), and afterward <b>and you shall screen the ark with the veil</b>, and so in the actual account (Exodus 40:20–21): \"and he placed the cover upon the ark above,\" \"and he brought the ark into the Tabernacle,\" and afterward \"and he put up the veil of the screen.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:16:52.539368316Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}